      "Ambroxan": "A modern molecule that gives a woody, ambery glow, used in tons of popular fragrances.",
      "Oud": "Dark resinous wood formed when agarwood trees are infected with mould.",
      "Vetiver": "Earthy grass root grown in places like Haiti, India and Java.",
      "Bergamot": "Citrus used in Earl Grey tea and countless colognes.",
      "Tonka bean": "Sweet seed with a hay, almond and vanilla scent.",
      "Patchouli": "Earthy leaf note from Southeast Asia, a hippie-era favourite.",
      "Musk": "Once animal-derived; today mostly made synthetically.",
      "Sandalwood": "Creamy wood; Mysore sandalwood is the most prized.",
      "Aldehydes": "Sparkly synthetic notes made famous by Chanel No 5.",
      "Orris": "Powdery note from iris roots, one of the costliest perfume materials.",
      "Oakmoss": "Mossy lichen note that gives chypre fragrances their forest-floor depth.",
      "Labdanum": "A sticky amber resin from the cistus shrub.",
      "Benzoin": "Sweet vanilla-like tree resin used as a fixative.",
      "Heliotrope": "Powdery almond and vanilla note from a purple flower.",
      "Osmanthus": "Apricot and leather-like flower from China.",
      "Castoreum": "Leathery note traditionally from beavers; now mostly recreated synthetically.",
      "Civet": "Warm animalic note once from civet cats; now mostly synthetic.",
      "Hedione": "Airy jasmine-like molecule famously used in Dior Eau Sauvage.",
      "Iso E Super": "Woody, velvety molecule that is the star of Molecule 01.",
      "Cashmeran": "Musky-woody molecule with a cosy, cashmere-like feel.",
      "Galbanum": "Bitter green resin used for sharp, crisp top notes.",
      "Opoponax": "Sweet resin, also known as sweet myrrh.",
      "Elemi": "Fresh, lemony-peppery tree resin.",
      "Immortelle": "Honeyed, maple-like note from the everlasting flower.",
      "Styrax": "Balsamic resin with a leathery, smoky sweetness.",
      "Tolu balsam": "Sweet balsamic resin from a South American tree.",
      "Davana": "Fruity, boozy-smelling Indian herb.",
      "Cistus": "The Mediterranean shrub whose resin gives labdanum.",
      "Coumarin": "Sweet hay-and-almond molecule found in tonka bean.",
      "Ambergris": "Rare waxy substance from sperm whales, used in perfume for centuries.",
      "Calone": "Synthetic molecule that gives the watery watermelon-ozone feel of 90s aquatics.",
      "Indole": "A heady molecule in jasmine and orange blossom that smells animalic when strong.",
      "Vanillin": "The main flavour molecule of vanilla, also made synthetically.",
      "Matcha": "Powdered green tea, a trendy gourmand and green note.",
      "Petrichor": "The earthy smell of rain on dry ground.",
      "Smell": "Technically what you do with it, but it's not a note."
